    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d521">

                <pb facs="0970" n="846" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg846"/>

                <head>No. 517.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hitt to Señor de
                    Zamacona.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 27,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Adverting to your note of July 25 last
                    concerning the alleged illegal arrest in Mexico of a fugitive criminal from
                    Arizona, I have now the honor to inclose for your information a copy of a letter
                    from the acting governor of the Territory of Arizona, of August 26 last, in
                    which it is stated that the proper steps would be taken to ascertain the facts
                    of the complaint.</p>
                <p>Adding that the inclosed communication has been received with a letter from the
                    Secretary of the Interior, of the 14th instant, I profit by this occasion to
                    renew to you, sir, the assurance of my highest consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>ROBERT R. HITT.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Acting
                        Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d521-a1.xml" xpointer="d521-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
